description:
FILED s539a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-13) from the #3823 census (docs/tap-assertion-audit.md "The Test::Builder methods"; probe scratch/s539a/pr/tbm.pl in the s539a worktree: perl's Test::Builder 1.302199 method list, `Test::Builder->can($m)` under PCL).

After s539a PCL answers 36 of perl's public methods (base 17).  STILL ABSENT, each needing NEW state (the brief's rule: a method that needs new state is filed, not built):
  child / create / finalize / reset / reset_outputs -- a second builder object (PCL's layer IS the one builder; a child would need its own counters, as `subtest` rebinds them);
  name -- the builder's name (the script name for the top builder);
  is_fh -- a handle predicate;
  find_TODO -- walks the caller's package for `$TODO` (caller fidelity, #233);
  todo_start / todo_end -- a TODO stack independent of `$TODO`;
  no_diag / no_ending / no_header / no_log_results / use_numbers -- output switches the layer has no flag for;
  coordinate_forks -- fork bookkeeping;
  context / ctx -- the Test2 bridge (Test2::API context objects).
Each call dies `Can't locate object method "X" via package "Test::Builder"` (rule 12), never a stub.  Build one when a board / everyday file reaches it (grep the board's `*PLAN*` / `*FILE*` rows for the method name).
